[4.8, "o", "  ARC Prize 2026 – ARC-AGI-3 (per the Kaggle\r\n  competition page):\r\n\r\n"]
[4.92, "o", "  Deadline\r\n  • Final submission: November 2, 2026, 23:59\r\n    UTC, about 31 days from today.\r\n"]
[5.04, "o", "  • Entry and team merger deadline: October\r\n    26, 2026. You must have joined by then.\r\n  • Winners announced: December 4, 2026.\r\n"]
[5.16, "o", "\r\n  One inconsistency on the entry cutoff:\r\n  Kaggle's structured field says 11:59 UTC on\r\n"]
[5.28, "o", "  October 26, while the timeline page says\r\n  times are 11:59 PM UTC. Treat the earlier\r\n  time as the safe one.\r\n"]
[5.4, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.8, "o", "  Metric: \"ARC-AGI-3 Metric\" (custom)\r\n  • Each game is scored from 0 to 100%.\r\n  • 100% means human-level performance: the\r\n"]
[10.92, "o", "    agent beat every game while matching the\r\n    number of actions humans took.\r\n  • Using fewer actions than humans does not\r\n"]
[11.04, "o", "    earn extra, because scores are capped at\r\n    100%.\r\n\r\n"]
[11.16, "o", "  It is a code competition (you submit a\r\n  notebook), limited to 1 submission per day.\r\n"]
